Custom numeric format strings

You can create a custom numeric format string, which consists of one or more custom numeric specifiers, to define how to format numeric data. A custom numeric format string is any format string that is not a standard numeric format string.

Custom numeric format strings are supported by some overloads of the ToString method of all numeric types. For example, you can supply a numeric format string to the System.Int32.ToString%28System.String%29 and System.Int32.ToString%28System.String%2CSystem.IFormatProvider%29 methods of the System.Int32 type. Custom numeric format strings are also supported by the .NET composite formatting feature, which is used by some Write and WriteLine methods of the System.Console and System.IO.StreamWriter classes, the System.String.Format*?displayProperty=nameWithType method, and the System.Text.StringBuilder.AppendFormat*?displayProperty=nameWithType method. String interpolation feature also supports custom numeric format strings.

Tip

You can download the Formatting Utility, a .NET Core Windows Forms application that lets you apply format strings to either numeric or date and time values and displays the result string. Source code is available for C# and Visual Basic.

