• Define an System.IDisposable implementation for unsubscribing.

The provider returns this implementation to subscribers so they can stop receiving notifications at any time. The following example defines a nested Unsubscriber class that receives a reference to the subscribers collection and to the subscriber when instantiated. The Unsubscriber class enables the subscriber to call the object's System.IDisposable.Dispose*?displayProperty=nameWithType implementation to remove itself from the subscribers collection.

    private sealed class Unsubscriber(
        List<IObserver<Temperature>> observers,
        IObserver<Temperature> observer,
        Lock sync) : IDisposable
    {
        public void Dispose()
        {
            lock (sync)
            {
                observers.Remove(observer);
            }
        }
    }

