Base class with unmanaged resources

Here's an example for implementing the dispose pattern for a base class that overrides System.Object.Finalize*?displayProperty=nameWithType in order to clean up unmanaged resources it owns. The example also demonstrates a way to implement Dispose(bool) in a thread-safe manner. Synchronization might be critical when dealing with unmanaged resources in a multi-threaded application. As mentioned earlier, this is an advanced scenario.

